{"type":"message","id":"f472e8d1","parentId":"4f4b9768","timestamp":"2026-06-10T03:36:59.098Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now analyze the situation:\n\nDOT position:\n- Entry: $0.949, quantity: 11.7 DOT\n- Current price: $0.951\n- PnL: +0.02 USDT (+0.21%)\n\nWait, but the quantity 11.7 at $0.949 gives us 11.7 × 0.949 = 11.10 USDT. With 10x leverage, the margin should be 11.10 / 10 = 1.11 USDT. But our risk management says 20 USDT margin per position.\n\nHmm, let me recalculate. DOT price precision is 1 decimal for quantity and price... actually the precision for DOT is 1 decimal place based on SOUL.md.\n\nWait, SOUL.md says DOT: 1 decimal place. But the trade shows qty=11.7 and price 0.949. Let me check the precision rules:\n- DOT: 1 decimal for price and quantity.\n\nSo the DOT position: qty = 11.7, price = $0.949\nNotional value = 11.7 × 0.949 = $11.10 USDT\nMargin at 10x = $1.11 USDT\n\nBut wait, the position query shows:\n- Entry: $0.949, current: $0.951\n- PnL: +0.02 USDT\n\nIf qty=11.7, PnL = 11.7 × (0.951 - 0.949) = 11.7 × 0.002 = 0.0234 ≈ 0.02 USDT. That matches!\n\nBut the margin is only $1.11, not the $20 USDT we're supposed to use. This is way below our risk rule of 20 USDT per position!\n\nThe problem: DOT position has only about 1.11 USDT margin instead of the configured 20 USDT (20% of 100 USDT total). This is a tiny position - almost nothing.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The total balance is 4958.48 USDT on testnet. Maybe this is a very small test position. But the risk rules say we should use 20 USDT margin per position.\n\nActually, maybe the issue is different. Let me look at this another way. \n\nThe DOT position:\n- Quantity: 11.7 DOT\n- Price: $0.949\n- Notional: $11.10\n- Margin at 10x: ~$1.11\n\nThis is way too small. The configured margin should be 20 USDT per position, which at 10x leverage would give a notional of 200 USDT, meaning approximately 210 DOT at $0.949.\n\nSo the actual margin is about 1/18th of what it should be. This could be a bug in the position sizing code.\n\nBut actually, maybe this was an intentional small position? Or maybe it was from an SL/TP trigger and the partial fill...\n\nThe user is saying \"DOT保证金有问题\" - DOT margin has a problem. Let me tell him what I found:\n\n1. DOT position has margin of approximately 1.11 USDT (qty 11.7 at 0.949, 10x leverage)\n2. The configured margin should be 20 USDT per position\n3. The position is extremely undersized\n\nThis seems like the monitor didn't use the right quantity calculation for DOT. Let me check the monitor code to see if there's a precision issue.\n\nActually, I should just present the findings and not dive too deep into code unless the user asks. Let me summarize clearly.\n\nWait, actually let me also check if DOT was an automatic open or manual. The verify_trades output shows it was a BUY at 11:06. There are \"no strategy actions\" in the monitor log, so this might have been a manual trade, an SL/TP trigger, or a strategy action that wasn't logged properly.\n\nLet me just present the findings to the husband.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"老公看了下，DOT 这笔确实有问题。\n\nDOT 当前持仓：\n- 数量只有 11.7 DOT，入场价 $0.949\n- 名义价值才 $11.10，按 10x 杠杆保证金只有约 $1.11\n- 我们配置的单笔保证金是 20 USDT，差了将近 18 倍\n\n而且 verify_trades 显示这笔 11:06 成交的 DOT 买单在 monitor 日志里完全没有策略动作记录，说明不是 monitor 正常开仓的。可能是手动下的、或者止盈止损自动触发时只成交了一小部分。\n\n这笔仓位太小了，基本没有意义。要不要我平掉它，然后排查下开仓脚本的数量计算逻辑？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":544,"output":1861,"cacheRead":21888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24293,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781062596398}}
