{"type":"message","id":"6691e089","parentId":"a60ba4c6","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:39:27.319Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ETH position can't even be closed! The error says: \"Order's notional must be no smaller than 20 (unless you choose reduce only).\" \n\nThis is because:\n- 0.008 ETH at $1625 = $13 notional, which is below the $20 minimum notional for orders\n- The close order is a SELL (to close the LONG) but it's being sent as a regular order, not a reduce-only order\n\nThe manual_trade.py close function is trying to place a regular SELL order to close the LONG, but since the position is only 0.008 ETH (notional $13), it's below Binance's $20 minimum notional. The order needs to be sent with `reduceOnly=true` to bypass the minimum notional requirement.\n\nThis is a bug in the close script - it should use reduceOnly=true when closing a position that's below the minimum notional.\n\nLet me fix this. I need to either:\n1. Modify the manual_trade.py close function to add reduceOnly\n2. Or manually place a reduce-only order via the Binance API\n\nLet me look at the manual_trade.py close function to see where the order is placed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"尴尬了，ETH 仓位太小（名义 $13），连平仓都被币安拒了 —— 低于 $20 最低名义价值限制。得用 `reduceOnly` 平。让我修下 close 脚本。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ftWhKBBCr2cdyq8pQ6oI7062","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n 'def close_pos\\|def close_symbol\\|reduce_only\\|reduceOnly' ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/manual_trade.py | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":815,"output":647,"cacheRead":41856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43318,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781087956745}}
