{"type":"message","id":"3805390e","parentId":"cf6d0475","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:40:29.558Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the position is in LONG position (BOTH mode). The positionAmt is 0.008 (positive = LONG). No open orders. But the ReduceOnly SELL was rejected.\n\nThe issue might be that when using reduceOnly in BOTH mode, Binance expects the order side to be the opposite of the position. For a LONG position (positionAmt positive), SELL should reduce it.\n\nBut -2022 \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" can also mean the order would increase rather than decrease the position. This happens in hedge mode (DUAL position mode where LONG and SHORT are on different sides).\n\nWait, `positionSide=BOTH` means the account is in one-way mode. In one-way mode:\n- LONG = positionAmt > 0\n- SHORT = positionAmt < 0\n- To close: use opposite side\n\nSo for ETH with positionAmt=0.008:\n- It's a LONG\n- To close: SELL\n- reduceOnly should work\n\nBut the error says it's rejected. Let me try closing without reduceOnly but with a different approach - maybe the issue is with the price formatting or something else.\n\nActually, let me look at what happened more carefully. The first close attempt (without reduceOnly) failed with -4164 (minimum notional $20). The second attempt (with reduceOnly) failed with -2022 (reduceOnly order rejected).\n\nLet me try placing the order directly with the Binance API, without going through the wrapper function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_DLOq3ff7MmHSfP7Oa4qu4817","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, get_signature, PROXIES, _api_key\nimport time, requests\n\ntimestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\nparams = {\n    'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n    'side': 'SELL',\n    'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': 0.008,\n    'reduceOnly': 'true',\n    'timestamp': timestamp,\n    'recvWindow': 30000\n}\nquery = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\nsig = get_signature(query)\nurl = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\nheaders = {'X-MBX-APIKEY': _api_key()}\nresp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\nprint(resp.json())\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":294,"output":913,"cacheRead":46848,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48055,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088016842}}
