{"type":"message","id":"ffd22db5","parentId":"479621f5","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:40:51.158Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even a raw API call gets the same -2022 error. This is very strange. The position is LONG (0.008 ETH) and we're sending a SELL reduceOnly order, which should reduce the position.\n\nLet me think about why this could happen:\n1. The position might not actually exist (maybe it was closed already by another means)\n2. The position might be in a different state\n\nLet me check the position more carefully and also check if there's some other issue with the account mode.\n\nActually wait - maybe the position is already being closed. The first attempt without reduceOnly might have actually created a partial fill or something. Let me check if there are any pending or partially filled orders.\n\nActually, looking back at the first attempt without reduceOnly, the error was -4164 (minimum notional $20), meaning the order was REJECTED and did NOT execute. So the position should still be intact.\n\nHmm, let me try another approach. Let me check if the account is in hedge mode and if there's a positionSide setting issue.\n\nActually, the Binance error -2022 can also mean that the reduceOnly order would leave the position with a very small amount that violates the minimum notional. Let me try closing the entire position using closePosition=true via the market order.\n\nWait, Binance doesn't support closePosition in market orders directly. But I can try to close the position by placing a limit order at a favorable price with reduceOnly.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach: the close_all_positions function from binance_auto_trade.py might work differently.\n\nLet me also check: maybe the issue is that the position was already partially filled by a previous order that I'm not seeing.\n\nLet me re-check the ETH position.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_BehelgSamQVMwFo5p1Dh4498","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request\nimport json\n\n# Check all positions again\npos = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk')\nfor p in (pos if isinstance(pos,list) else []):\n    amt = float(p.get('positionAmt',0) or 0)\n    if abs(amt) > 0:\n        print(f'{p[\\\"symbol\\\"]}: amt={amt}, entry={p[\\\"entryPrice\\\"]}, PN={p[\\\"unRealizedProfit\\\"]}, isolated={p[\\\"isolatedWallet\\\"]}, posSide={p.get(\\\"positionSide\\\",\\\"?\\\")}')\n\n# Check account positions\nacc = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/account')\nif 'positions' in acc:\n    for p in acc['positions']:\n        amt = float(p.get('positionAmt',0) or 0)\n        if abs(amt) > 0:\n            print(f'ACCT {p[\\\"symbol\\\"]}: amt={amt}, isolated={p.get(\\\"isolatedWallet\\\", \\\"?\\\")}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":283,"output":1053,"cacheRead":47616,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48952,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088035140}}
