{"type":"message","id":"3139c1af","parentId":"0fc4d435","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:41:23.242Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ETH position definitely exists: amt=0.008, posSide=BOTH. All positions are in BOTH mode (one-way mode).\n\nThe error -2022 \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" when trying to SELL 0.008 ETH with reduceOnly=true is puzzling.\n\nLet me think about this differently. In one-way (BOTH) mode:\n- positionAmt > 0 = LONG\n- positionAmt < 0 = SHORT\n\nFor ETH: positionAmt = 0.008. That's positive, so it's LONG.\nTo close it: SELL with reduceOnly=true.\n\nBut -2022 means the order would NOT reduce the position. This could happen if:\n1. The account is somehow treating it as a SHORT (but the positionAmt is clearly positive)\n2. There's a bug in Binance testnet\n\nWait, let me check something. Is the position having issues because the position amount 0.008 is so small that even the reduceOnly order can't fully close it? \n\nActually, let me try using `closePosition: true` instead. In Binance futures API, you can use `closePosition: \"true\"` to close the entire position.\n\nActually no, `closePosition` is only available in v2 order endpoint and is used with `positionSide`. Let me try another approach.\n\nWait, I know what might be happening. Let me check if there's a hedge mode / dual position mode issue. In some Binance configurations, even though positions show as BOTH, the API might require positionSide specification.\n\nActually, let me try closing the position by buying enough to make notional > $20 first, then close without reduceOnly. The close_position function in crypto_signal_monitor.py already has this logic at line 1322-1328!\n\nFrom the code I read earlier:\n```python\n# 降级3：名义价值 < $20 → 买入≥$20 名义价值的量撑大后全平\nnotional = qty * current_price\nif notional < 20:\n    pad_qty = 20.0 / current_price  # 最少买入 $20 名义价值\n```\n\nLet me do this manually - buy enough ETH to make the position notional > $20, then close the whole thing.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"ETH 有持仓但 reduceOnly 被拒，可能是 Binance 测试网对这个超小仓位有 bug。我用另一种方式：先补到 $20 名义以上再全平。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_SlwvXnX5qvWzeDJiBjgC8701","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, get_signature, PROXIES, _api_key\nimport time, requests\n\n# ETH mark price\nticker = requests.get('https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/ticker/price?symbol=ETHUSDT', proxies=PROXIES, verify=False).json()\nprice = float(ticker['price'])\nprint(f'ETH price: {price}')\n\n# We have 0.008 ETH. To get notional > \\$20, we need total qty > 20/price\n# Current notional = 0.008 * price = about \\$13. Need to add about \\$7+\n# Buy additional: 8/price ETH\npad_qty = 8.0 / price  \n# Round to 3 decimal places (ETH precision)\npad_qty = round(pad_qty, 3)\nprint(f'Padding buy: {pad_qty} ETH')\n\n# Buy more ETH\ntimestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\nparams = {\n    'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n    'side': 'BUY',\n    'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': pad_qty,\n    'timestamp': timestamp,\n    'recvWindow': 30000\n}\nquery = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\nsig = get_signature(query)\nurl = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\nheaders = {'X-MBX-APIKEY': _api_key()}\nresp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\nresult = resp.json()\nprint(f'Buy result: {result}')\n\nif result.get('orderId'):\n    # Now total should be > \\$20 notional. Close whole position.\n    time.sleep(2)\n    # Get new position size\n    pos = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\n    if isinstance(pos, list) and len(pos) > 0:\n        total_qty = abs(float(pos[0].get('positionAmt', 0) or 0))\n        print(f'Total ETH position: {total_qty}')\n        \n        timestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\n        params = {\n            'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n            'side': 'SELL',\n            'type': 'MARKET',\n            'quantity': total_qty,\n            'timestamp': timestamp,\n            'recvWindow': 30000\n        }\n        query = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\n        sig = get_signature(query)\n        url = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\n        resp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\n        print(f'Close result: {resp.json()}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":542,"output":1738,"cacheRead":48512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":50792,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088058414}}
