{"type":"message","id":"4c162bbe","parentId":"48df2a1a","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:41:43.555Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Of course! 0.005 ETH at $1624 = only $8.12 notional, which is below the $20 minimum. I can't buy more because any increment would also be too small.\n\nSo the only way to close this position is with reduceOnly. But reduceOnly keeps getting rejected with -2022.\n\nLet me think about why -2022 is happening...\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the error message: \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected.\" This is a Binance testnet issue. On testnet, sometimes reduceOnly orders are rejected for very small positions.\n\nLet me try another approach: There might be a way to close the position using the position management functions. Let me try using close_all_positions from binance_auto_trade.py, or try setting a STOP_MARKET order with closePosition=true, which is supported for algo orders.\n\nActually, let me try the algo order approach - place a STOP_MARKET order with closePosition=true at a price that will immediately trigger.\n\nWait, actually, let me try one more thing. Maybe the issue is that Binance testnet's reduceOnly doesn't work well with MARKET orders for tiny positions. Let me try a LIMIT order instead.\n\nOr better yet, let me try using positionSide= specification. If we specify positionSide=LONG explicitly, maybe reduceOnly will work.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_IEPuW9dowo4RxjqPIWsL3524","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, get_signature, PROXIES, _api_key\nimport time, requests\n\ntimestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\n# Try with explicit positionSide\nparams = {\n    'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n    'side': 'SELL',\n    'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': 0.008,\n    'reduceOnly': 'true',\n    'positionSide': 'LONG',\n    'timestamp': timestamp,\n    'recvWindow': 30000\n}\nquery = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\nsig = get_signature(query)\nurl = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\nheaders = {'X-MBX-APIKEY': _api_key()}\nresp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\nprint('Market+LONG:', resp.json())\n\n# Try LIMIT order with reduceOnly\ntimestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\nparams2 = {\n    'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n    'side': 'SELL',\n    'type': 'LIMIT',\n    'quantity': 0.008,\n    'price': 1620,  # slightly below market to ensure it fills\n    'timeInForce': 'GTC',\n    'reduceOnly': 'true',\n    'timestamp': timestamp,\n    'recvWindow': 30000\n}\nquery2 = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params2.items()])\nsig2 = get_signature(query2)\nurl2 = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query2}&signature={sig2}'\nresp2 = requests.post(url2, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\nprint('Limit:', resp2.json())\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":285,"output":1067,"cacheRead":50304,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51656,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088088730}}
