{"type":"message","id":"ccb97ada","parentId":"3844638d","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:42:05.995Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! When using positionSide=LONG, the error changed to -1106: \"Parameter 'reduceonly' sent when not required.\" This means when you specify positionSide, the position is being treated differently (hedge mode vs one-way mode).\n\nIn one-way mode (BOTH), we can't use positionSide - that's only for hedge mode. And in one-way mode, the reduceOnly -2022 error persists.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. Let me check if Binance testnet has a \"close position\" mechanism. On the real Binance, you can use fapi/v1/order with:\n- In one-way mode: just SELL the full amount for a LONG position\n\nWait, the issue is that the notional is below $20. Let me try using the `closePosition` parameter which is available in the v2 endpoint.\n\nActually, I just realized something: maybe the TESTNET has stricter rules than mainnet for tiny positions. Let me try another approach:\n\n1. Open a new ETH position with the proper size (0.123 ETH), which would make the total > $20 notional\n2. Then immediately close everything\n\nOr... I could try something else. Let me check if we can use `closePosition=true` in the v2 order endpoint.\n\nWait, actually, let me re-read the Binance documentation. The `positionSide` parameter with `reduceOnly` might work differently. Let me try:\n- Without positionSide (BOTH mode)\n- SELL with reduceOnly=false and an amount that covers the full position but makes notional >= $20\n\nBut we have 0.008 ETH. To get notional >= $20, we'd need to increase the quantity... which we can't because each buy would be below $20.\n\nActually, what if I combine approaches? \n1. Cancel any SL/TP orders\n2. Buy more ETH in a way that accumulates past $20\n3. Then close the full lot\n\nWait, each individual BUY would be below $20 notional, so they'd all be rejected without reduceOnly. And reduceOnly BUY wouldn't apply since we're already LONG.\n\nHmm, this is a chicken-and-egg problem. The position is stuck.\n\nLet me try one more thing: use close_all_positions from binance_auto_trade.py, which might have different logic.\n\nActually, let me check what close_all_positions does.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_cbwsvWeCkLkg6yf52d8w5013","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n 'def close_all_positions' ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_mKw0i5yMizLnPcVxcYrN5517","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":365,"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py","limit":100}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":321,"output":1173,"cacheRead":51328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52822,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088110285}}
{"type":"message","id":"bf355316","parentId":"ccb97ada","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:42:06.179Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_cbwsvWeCkLkg6yf52d8w5013","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"363:def close_all_positions():"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":103,"aggregated":"363:def close_all_positions():","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1781088126166}}
{"type":"message","id":"0774f25d","parentId":"bf355316","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:42:06.198Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_mKw0i5yMizLnPcVxcYrN5517","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    平仓所有持仓（爆仓保护用）\n    \"\"\"\n    positions = get_all_positions()\n    for pos in positions:\n        try:\n            symbol = pos['symbol'] + \"USDT\"\n            amt = float(pos.get('amount', 0))\n            if amt != 0:\n                side = 'SELL' if amt > 0 else 'BUY'\n                qty = abs(amt)\n                place_order(symbol, side, qty)\n                log.info(f\"✅ 爆仓保护平仓 {symbol} {side} {qty}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            log.error(f\"❌ 爆仓保护平仓失败 {symbol}: {e}\")\n\ndef cancel_algo_orders(symbol: str):\n    \"\"\"取消某币种全部 Algo 条件单（TP/SL）\n    \n    2026-06-05 修复：旧版用 /algoOpenOrders 批量删不生效，\n    改为先列后逐笔删，确保清理彻底。\n    \"\"\"\n    sym_usdt = f\"{symbol}USDT\" if not symbol.endswith(\"USDT\") else symbol\n    results = []\n    try:\n        # 1. 列出所有 algo 单\n        open_algos = request(\"GET\", \"/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders\", {\"symbol\": sym_usdt})\n        if not isinstance(open_algos, list):\n            log.warning(f\"⚠️ {symbol} 列出 Algo 单失败：{open_algos}\")\n            return results\n        \n        # 2. 逐笔取消\n        for o in open_algos:\n            algo_id = o.get('algoId')\n            if algo_id:\n                del_result = request(\"DELETE\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOrder\", {\"algoId\": algo_id})\n                results.append(del_result)\n                if isinstance(del_result, dict) and del_result.get('code') == '200':\n                    log.info(f\"🗑️ {symbol} Algo 单已取消 algoId={algo_id}\")\n                elif isinstance(del_result, dict) and del_result.get('code') in (-2011,):\n                    # 单已被取消（不存在），正常情况\n                    log.info(f\"🗑️ {symbol} Algo 单 algoId={algo_id} 已不存在（跳过）\")\n                else:\n                    log.warning(f\"⚠️ {symbol} Algo 单取消失败 algoId={algo_id}: {del_result}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.error(f\"❌ {symbol} 取消 Algo 单异常：{e}\")\n    return results\n\n\ndef place_algo_conditional_order(\n    symbol: str,\n    side: str,\n    order_type: str,\n    trigger_price,\n    working_type: str = \"MARK_PRICE\",\n    quantity: float = None,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    币安 USD-M 条件单（2025-12 起须走 Algo API，否则 -4120）\n\n    order_type: STOP_MARKET（止损）| TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET（止盈）\n    side: 平仓方向 — 平多 SELL，平空 BUY\n    quantity: 精确数量（传了就用 reduceOnly+quantity，不传保留旧行为 closePosition=true）\n    2026-06-04 修复：closePosition=true 在测试网算出错误数量，改为传入精确 quantity\n    2026-06-05 修复：triggerPrice 按 symbol 精度格式化，替代全局 format_price（DOT -1111 bug）\n    \"\"\"\n    sym = symbol.replace(\"USDT\", \"\")\n    # 按币种价格精度格式化触发价\n    price_prec = get_price_precision(sym)\n    formatted_trigger = round(trigger_price, price_prec)\n    \n    params = {\n        \"algoType\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n        \"symbol\": symbol,\n        \"side\": side,\n        \"type\": order_type,\n        \"triggerPrice\": formatted_trigger,\n        \"workingType\": working_type,\n    }\n    if quantity is not None:\n        sym = symbol.replace(\"USDT\", \"\")\n        params[\"quantity\"] = str(format_quantity(sym, quantity, 0))\n        params[\"reduceOnly\"] = \"true\"\n    else:\n        params[\"closePosition\"] = \"true\"\n    return request(\"POST\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOrder\", params)\n\n\ndef check_margin_ratio_protection():\n    \"\"\"\n    爆仓保护检查\n    保证金率低于 5% 立即平仓所有持仓\n    \"\"\"\n    margin_ratio = get_margin_ratio()\n    threshold = RISK.get(\"margin_ratio_warning\", 0.05)\n    \n    if margin_ratio < threshold:\n        log.warning(f\"🚨 爆仓保护触发！保证金率={margin_ratio:.4f} < {threshold:.4f}\")\n        close_all_positions()\n        log.critical(\"⚠️ 保证金率过低，已强制平仓所有持仓\")\n        return True\n\n[189 more lines in file. Use offset=465 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1781088126179}}
{"type":"message","id":"b378ef73","parentId":"0774f25d","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:42:25.476Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that close_all_positions just calls place_order(symbol, side, qty) without reduce_only. So it would also fail with -4164 for ETH's tiny position.\n\nLet me try a different approach. Let me check if I can use the `closePosition` parameter in the algo order or try to adjust the position by first closing the SL/TP orders and then trying reduceOnly again.\n\nActually, wait. Let me look at the fapi/v1/positionMargin endpoint. On Binance, you can add margin to an isolated position to increase its isolated wallet. If I add more margin, maybe the position can then be closed.\n\nNo wait, that won't help - the issue is the NOTIONAL value, not the margin.\n\nOK let me think of another approach. On Binance testnet, there might be a way to close a position below minimum notional. Let me try:\n\n1. Using `closePosition: true` in the v2 order API\n2. Or try setting the position to dual-position mode temporarily\n\nActually, let me try something simpler. What if I open a new LONG position for ETH with the correct size? That would be adding to the existing 0.008 ETH position. The new order would need to be at least $20 notional.\n\nNew order: BUY 0.123 ETH at ~$1624 = $200 notional. That's well above $20 minimum.\n\nThen I'd have 0.008 + 0.123 = 0.131 ETH. Then close all 0.131 ETH without reduceOnly.\n\nWait, but the total capital is $100 and I should respect that. Let me calculate: 0.131 ETH at $1624 = $213 notional, at 10x = $21.3 margin. That's slightly over the $20 per-position limit. But close enough.\n\nActually, that won't work either - because the whole purpose is to fix the position, not increase it. The proper approach is to just close it.\n\nLet me try another thing: maybe the reduceOnly issue is specific to Binance TESTNET. Let me search for testnet-specific quirks with reduceOnly.\n\nActually, you know what, let me try one more creative approach. In Binance, if you use the Hedge Mode (dual position mode) instead of One-Way mode, you can specify positionSide and use closePosition. But switching mode might be complex.\n\nLet me try yet another approach: create a STOP_MARKET order with closePosition=true at a price that will trigger immediately (current price, which for a market stop order basically means it triggers right away).\n\nIn the place_algo_conditional_order function, when quantity is None, it uses closePosition=true. Let me try that.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_5LC6FyiC9xeUVCBINeHc1597","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, place_algo_conditional_order\nimport time\n\n# Try closePosition=true algo order\n# For ETH LONG: SELL STOP_MARKET at current price (will trigger immediately)\nticker_result = request('GET', '/fapi/v1/ticker/price', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\nprice = float(ticker_result['price'])\nprint(f'ETH price: {price}')\n\n# Place STOP_MARKET with closePosition=true, trigger slightly above current\nresult = place_algo_conditional_order(\n    'ETHUSDT', \n    'SELL', \n    'STOP_MARKET', \n    price * 0.99,  # trigger slightly below current to execute immediately\n    working_type='MARK_PRICE',\n    quantity=None  # use closePosition=true\n)\nprint(f'Algo order result: {result}')\n\n# Wait and check\ntime.sleep(3)\npos = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\nif isinstance(pos, list) and len(pos) > 0:\n    amt = float(pos[0].get('positionAmt', 0) or 0)\n    print(f'ETH position after: {amt}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1212,"output":1500,"cacheRead":52224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":54936,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopR