{"type":"message","id":"ebaabd31","parentId":"0acdc6e7","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:43:21.664Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The algo order was created but didn't trigger because the trigger price ($1609.03) is below the current price ($1625.28). For a STOP_MARKET SELL, it triggers when the price goes DOWN through the trigger price. Since the stop price is below market, it won't trigger.\n\nWait, actually for a STOP_MARKET SELL (closing a LONG), the trigger works as follows:\n- When mark price ≤ trigger price, the order is triggered\n- But $1609 is below $1625, so it should already be triggered... unless Binance treats it differently\n\nActually, on Binance, for STOP_MARKET:\n- BUY STOP: triggers when price goes ABOVE stop price\n- SELL STOP: triggers when price goes BELOW stop price\n\nSince the order was created successfully and the trigger price is $1609 (below $1625 current), it should trigger when price falls to $1609. But we want it to trigger immediately.\n\nLet me try the opposite - use a TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET with a trigger below current price, which would trigger immediately.\n\nFor TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET:\n- BUY TAKE_PROFIT: triggers when price goes ABOVE trigger\n- SELL TAKE_PROFIT: triggers when price goes BELOW trigger\n\nWait, that's the same as STOP_MARKET for SELL. Both trigger when price goes below trigger for SELL.\n\nHmm, let me try setting the trigger above current price. For a SELL TAKE_PROFIT:\n- It triggers when price goes ABOVE trigger price... wait, no.\n\nActually, for Binance:\n- STOP_MARKET SELL: triggers when mark price ≤ trigger price (price falling through stop)\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL: triggers when mark price ≥ trigger price (price rising through take profit)\n\nSo for a SELL to close LONG:\n- STOP_MARKET SELL: set trigger below market, triggers when price falls\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL: set trigger above market, triggers when price rises\n\nIf I want it to trigger immediately, I should:\n- Use STOP_MARKET SELL with trigger ABOVE market (like $1700) - wait, that won't work because stop is for falling prices\n- Use TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL with trigger BELOW market - that won't work either because TP is for rising prices\n\nHmm, actually on Binance Futures:\n- STOP_MARKET: \"BUY stop market: buy when market price >= stop price. SELL stop market: sell when market price <= stop price\"\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET: \"BUY take profit market: buy when market price <= take profit price. SELL take profit market: sell when market price >= take profit price\"\n\nWait, that's different! Let me re-check:\n- STOP_MARKET SELL: trigger when price <= stopPrice (falling price = stop loss)\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL: trigger when price >= profitPrice (rising price = take profit)\n\nSo:\n- To trigger a SELL immediately (current ≈ $1625):\n  - STOP_MARKET SELL: set trigger at $1630+ (above current, so price would have to go UP through it to trigger... no, stop triggers when price goes DOWN through it)\n  \nActually, I think I got confused. Let me just set the trigger price to something that's guaranteed to trigger. For a STOP_MARKET SELL, the trigger is when the price falls through the stop. So I need to set the stop ABOVE the current price to trigger immediately... wait no.\n\nLet me think again:\n- STOP_MARKET SELL = \"sell when price drops to stop level\". So if current is $1625 and stop is $1610, it triggers when price falls to $1610. But we want immediate trigger, so we'd set stop at $1630 (above market), which means... does it trigger immediately since the price already crossed that level?\n\nActually no. On Binance, STOP_MARKET orders only trigger on price movements. If you set stop at $1630 SELL and price is currently $1625, the price hasn't \"crossed\" the stop from above, so it won't trigger until it goes up to $1630 and then back down through it.\n\nSo the way to trigger immediately:\n- STOP_MARKET BUY with trigger BELOW market: price is above trigger, and for BUY stop, it triggers when price >= stop price. Since current ($1625) >= trigger (say $800), it should trigger immediately on BUY.\n\nBut we need a SELL to close a LONG. So:\n- SELL TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET: triggers when price >= take profit price\n- Set take profit at $0.01 - price is way above, should trigger immediately!\n\nWait no, that's for BUY take profit. Let me double check:\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL: triggers when price >= profit price\n\nIf current is $1625 and I set profit price to $800... does it trigger immediately? Let me think... Yes! Because the price ($1625) is already above the trigger ($800), the condition is met and it should trigger right away.\n\nActually wait, I'm not sure about this. Let me just try setting the trigger to a price that would definitely trigger. Let me try TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET with trigger at $800, which is well below current. If SELL TAKE_PROFIT triggers when price >= trigger, then yes it should trigger immediately.\n\nHmm, actually for TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL in Binance futures:\n- Triggers when mark price rises to or above the stop price\n- Set trigger at $0.01: current $1625 is way above, so it triggers!\n\nLet me try this.\n\nWait, actually I realize for algo orders, Binance might enforce that the trigger price must be at a \"reasonable\" distance from the current price. Let me check.\n\nActually, looking at the code comment: \"2026-06-04 修复：closePosition=true 在测试网算出错误数量\". The closePosition=true was previously problematic on testnet because it calculated wrong quantities. This is exactly what's happening here.\n\nBut the algo order DID succeed with closePosition=true. It was created with quantity=\"0.000\" and closePosition=True. The issue is that the trigger hasn't been hit yet.\n\nLet me cancel that algo order and try with a trigger that will fire immediately - use TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL with a low trigger.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_n8O1Rx2ITWM0n2fWnSNY7452","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, place_algo_conditional_order\nimport time\n\n# Cancel the previous algo order\nrequest('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOrder', {'algoId': 1000000101361520})\nprint('Cancelled previous algo')\n\n# Try TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL with trigger at \\$600 (way below current \\$1625)\n# SELL TAKE_PROFIT triggers when price >= trigger → should fire immediately\nprice = 1625\ntrigger = 600.0\nresult = place_algo_conditional_order(\n    'ETHUSDT', \n    'SELL', \n    'TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET', \n    trigger,\n    working_type='MARK_PRICE',\n    quantity=None  # use closePosition=true\n)\nprint(f'TP order result: {result}')\n\ntime.sleep(5)\npos = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\nif isinstance(pos, list) and len(pos) > 0:\n    amt = float(pos[0].get('positionAmt', 0) or 0)\n    pn = pos[0].get('unRealizedProfit', 0)\n    print(f'ETH position: amt={amt}, PN={pn}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":669,"output":3201,"cacheRead":54400,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58270,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088159383}}
