{"type":"message","id":"bcf25ce8","parentId":"2b3cb7e2","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:44:02.511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\"Order would immediately trigger\" - this is expected. Binance rejects TP/SL orders that would trigger instantly since that could be used for market manipulation. \n\nOK so algorithms orders are not the solution for instant execution. Let me think of another approach.\n\nWait, I just realized something. Let me check the actual issue more carefully. The place_order function sends `reduceOnly` as a string \"true\"/\"false\". But the Binance API parameter might be case-sensitive or formatted differently.\n\nActually, looking at the place_order code:\n```python\norder_params = {\n    \"symbol\": symbol,\n    \"side\": side,\n    \"type\": \"MARKET\",\n    \"quantity\": formatted_quantity,\n    \"reduceOnly\": str(reduce_only).lower()\n}\n```\n\nThis sends `reduceOnly: \"true\"` which should be fine.\n\nHmm, let me try using the `reduceOnly: true` with the actual current position amount, but in the v2 API endpoint.\n\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. Let me try to close it by adding more to the position first, then closing the whole thing. But as we saw, we can't BUY more because any individual buy would be below $20 notional.\n\nWait... what if I try to BUY using reduceOnly=false but with a larger quantity? But our position is 0.008 ETH and minimum notional is $20 for new orders. To buy $20 notional, I need $20/$1625 = 0.0123 ETH. But that's a NEW position, not reduceOnly, so it should work... wait no, it would fail because it's not reduceOnly and the notional would be $20+.\n\nHmm wait, I tried 0.005 ETH which was $8 notional. What if I try 0.015 ETH? That would be $24.36 notional, above $20 minimum.\n\nLet me try: BUY 0.013 ETH (0.013 * 1625 = $21.13 notional, above $20 minimum).\n\nThen total position = 0.008 + 0.013 = 0.021 ETH, notional = $34.13\nThen SELL 0.021 ETH (notional = $34.13, above $20), without reduceOnly.\n\nThis should work! Let me try this.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_oJ4UcRl07URd497yFIyd5940","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, get_signature, PROXIES, _api_key, get_quantity_precision\nimport time, requests\n\nheaders = {'X-MBX-APIKEY': _api_key()}\n\n# Get current price\nticker = requests.get('https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/ticker/price?symbol=ETHUSDT', proxies=PROXIES, verify=False).json()\nprice = float(ticker['price'])\nprint(f'ETH price: {price}')\n\n# Add to position: buy enough to make total notional > \\$20\n# Current: 0.008 ETH = about \\$13\n# Need to add at least \\$7 more → 0.005 ETH, but \\$8 notional < \\$20 minimum\n# Instead buy the \\$20 minimum: \\$20/price ≈ 0.013 ETH\nadd_qty = round(20.0 / price, 3)\nprint(f'Adding {add_qty} ETH (\\${add_qty * price:.2f} notional)')\n\ntimestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\nparams = {\n    'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n    'side': 'BUY',\n    'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': add_qty,\n    'timestamp': timestamp,\n    'recvWindow': 30000\n}\nquery = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\nsig = get_signature(query)\nurl = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\nresp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\nbuy_result = resp.json()\nprint(f'Buy: {buy_result}')\n\nif buy_result.get('orderId'):\n    time.sleep(2)\n    # Now close entire position\n    pos = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\n    total = abs(float(pos[0].get('positionAmt', 0) or 0))\n    print(f'Total ETH: {total}')\n\n    timestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    params = {\n        'symbol': 'ETHUSDT',\n        'side': 'SELL',\n        'type': 'MARKET',\n        'quantity': total,\n        'timestamp': timestamp,\n        'recvWindow': 30000\n    }\n    query = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\n    sig = get_signature(query)\n    url = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\n    resp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\n    print(f'Close: {resp.json()}')\nelse:\n    # Try 0.015 instead\n    add_qty = 0.015\n    print(f'Trying {add_qty} ETH (\\${add_qty * price:.2f} notional)')\n    timestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    params['quantity'] = add_qty\n    params['timestamp'] = timestamp\n    query = '&'.join([f'{k}={v}' for k,v in params.items()])\n    sig = get_signature(query)\n    url = f'https://testnet.binancefuture.com/fapi/v1/order?{query}&signature={sig}'\n    resp = requests.post(url, headers=headers, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\n    print(f'Buy2: {resp.json()}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":398,"output":1857,"cacheRead":56960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59215,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088216184}}
