an_symbols and AUTO_TRADE_ENABLED:\n                        for sym in orphan_symbols:\n                            try:\n                                cancel_algo_orders(f\"{sym}USDT\")\n                                log.info(f\"🗑️ 清理孤儿 Algo 单：{sym}\")\n                            except Exception:\n                                pass\n                    positions = new_positions\n                    save_positions(positions)\n                    log.info(f\"✅ 持仓同步完成：{len(positions)}个\")\n                    # 🐛 仓位反转修复：重建后提交止盈止损 Algo 单\n                    for pos in positions:\n                        submit_initial_algo_orders(pos)\n\n[316 more lines in file. Use offset=2490 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1781088926780}}
{"type":"message","id":"c284bac0","parentId":"7b73e204","timestamp":"2026-06-10T10:55:48.454Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed! This is the bug. The reconstruction code at line 2453-2475:\n\n1. Detects a tiny position on Binance (e.g., 0.008 ETH, nominal ~$13)\n2. Calculates the correct amount: 0.123 ETH (per risk rules)\n3. Updates the LOCAL CACHE to have amount=0.123 \n4. Submits Algo orders (SL/TP) for the correct amount\n\nBut it NEVER actually places an order to INCREASE the Binance position from 0.008 to 0.123 ETH!\n\nThe fix needs to:\n1. When the API shows a position smaller than the expected size (but still > $5 notional), either:\n   a. Close the tiny position and reopen with correct size\n   b. Add to the position to reach correct size\n   \nOption (b) is cleaner - just place a BUY/SELL order for the difference.\n\nLet me now understand the full flow better. The positions on Binance that are too small could come from:\n1. Partial fills during close operations\n2. SL/TP algo orders that only partially filled\n3. Manual trades\n\nThe fix should be in the reconstruction code: when `abs(amt)` is significantly different from `correct_amount`, place an adjustment order.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The `submit_initial_algo_orders` function submits SL/TP orders. If the Binance position is 0.008 ETH but the SL/TP orders are for 0.123 ETH, the SL/TP orders might fail or cause issues.\n\nThe right fix:\n1. In the reconstruction loop, compare API amount with expected amount\n2. If API amount < expected amount (by a significant margin), close the tiny position and reopen with correct size\n3. This ensures consistency between Binance and local cache\n\nLet me implement this fix. I'll modify the reconstruction code to:\n- When API amount differs significantly from expected, close the position and reopen\n\nActually, a cleaner approach:\n- When rebuilding, if the API position size is substantially different from what it should be, close and reopen it\n\nLet me write the fix.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到根因了。看这段重建代码：\n\n```python\n# 第 2453 行：检测到 Binance 上的持仓\ncorrect_amount = format_quantity(symbol, expected_qty, entry)\n# 只更新了本地缓存！\nnew_positions.append({..., 'amount': correct_amount, ...})\n```\n\n**本地缓存写的是正确数量（0.123 ETH），但 Binance 上实际只有 0.008 ETH —— 中间没有下任何单去补足！**\n\n流程是这样的：\n1. 某个事件产生了迷你仓位（SL/TP 部分成交、残留等）\n2. Monitor 同步 API 时检测到方向变化/数量异常\n3. 重建逻辑把**本地缓存**改成了风控标准量\n4. 但从来没有向币安下过补仓单\n5. Monitor 自以为仓位 OK，跳过开仓\n6. 迷你仓一直在那挂着\n\n修法：重建时如果 API 实际量跟风控标准差距大，先平掉迷你仓再用正确量重开。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Ii8cnHgdhxzHiNxmT8MP0929","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":2448,"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","limit":45}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":651,"output":1221,"cacheRead":74752,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76624,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781088926812}}
